#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-auto: run `claude` and, when the context reaches a threshold, continue in a NEW session started from a
compact-handoff note, in the same terminal window. Claude Code's own compaction is not involved.

    claude-auto [claude args...]    run claude (interactive); every argument goes to claude unchanged
    claude-auto __hook              internal: the hook that claude-auto adds with --settings

How it works
  1. The wrapper writes a settings file with the PreToolUse, Stop, PostToolUse, SubagentStart and SubagentStop hooks and runs
     `claude --settings <file> ...` in the foreground of this terminal. Those hooks are added to your own;
     ~/.claude/settings.json is never touched, and sessions started with plain `claude` are not affected (the hook
     acts only when CLAUDE_AUTO_RUN is set).
  2. The hook reads the context size of the last request from the transcript (input + cache_read + cache_creation
     tokens). Under the threshold it does nothing. At or over it, it runs the compact-handoff skill's make_context.py,
     saves what the transcript does not hold yet (pending/ next to HANDOFF.md) and drops run/signal.json.
  3. PostToolUse also answers continue:false, so the old session does no more work. The wrapper sees signal.json, ends
     claude (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL), restores the terminal and runs `claude "Citește …/HANDOFF.md …"` in the same window.
  Not wrapped (run as plain claude): -p/--print, --version, --help, --bg and the claude subcommands (mcp, doctor, ...).

The transcript is written AFTER the hooks of an event (measured: a Bash tool_result showed up 9 s after the call), so the
last tool result (PostToolUse) or the last reply (Stop) comes from the hook's own payload and is saved, whole and in pieces
one Read can open, in pending/ next to HANDOFF.md. Hooks of parallel tool calls that lose the claim save theirs too. The
first Stop of a run sees 0 tokens (no usage record is in the transcript yet), so a Stop handoff needs a second turn.
A --settings of your own is merged with the hooks (claude uses only the last --settings it gets).
Subagents: their hook events carry an agent_id and the session's own session_id and transcript_path, and ending claude ends
them. So an event with an agent_id never starts a handoff; SubagentStart/SubagentStop and each tool call of a subagent keep
run/agents/<agent_id> up to date, and while one was active within CLAUDE_AUTO_AGENT_IDLE seconds the handoff waits (one line
in auto.log) for the next event of the session after the last SubagentStop, up to CLAUDE_AUTO_DEFER_EXTRA tokens above the
threshold. A background launch and a SendMessage that resumes a finished subagent mark it, and TaskStop unmarks it (claude sends
no SubagentStop for that), each at its own PostToolUse. Not covered: a background subagent whose finish has not reached the transcript yet, and processes that are not subagents.

Env (all optional)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_TOKENS         threshold in tokens (default 150000)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_PRETOOL_MARGIN tokens before the threshold where a tool is blocked and handed off first (default 30000;
                             0 disables this guard). It avoids admitting a large tool result to an almost-full session.
  CLAUDE_AUTO_NEXT_ARGS      flags for the follow-up sessions, e.g. "--permission-mode acceptEdits". Default: the
                             --permission-mode/... flags you started with (see STICKY), with --model and --effort
                             of the session that is closed (read from its transcript, so a /model or /effort made
                             during the session carries over). When set, the whole value is used as it is.
  CLAUDE_AUTO_ANCHOR_ID      immutable, already-warmed Claude session ID. When set, every handoff resumes a fork of
                             this anchor, then appends HANDOFF.md; without it, the normal new-session handoff is used.
  CLAUDE_AUTO_RULE           off (or 0) stops claude-auto from appending the variant-check rule to the system prompt of
                             every session it starts (default on; skipped when you pass your own --append-system-prompt
                             or --append-system-prompt-file)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_SKILLS         which skills the new session loads again from the one that is closed: none (default; the
                             handoff carries no skill text), all (every skill the old session loaded), or NAME,NAME
                             (only those, whole names as make_context.py --list-skills prints them, e.g.
                             "apana:logic-test-debug,android-cli"; a name the old session did not load is left out and logged)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_MAX            handoffs per run (default 0 = unlimited); after that claude runs without the hook
  CLAUDE_AUTO_COOLDOWN       seconds between two handoffs of one run (default 60: limits the frequency if the new session
                             is itself over the threshold because the note is large)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_AGENT_IDLE     seconds without any event of a subagent after which it no longer holds the handoff back (default 900)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_DEFER_EXTRA    tokens above the threshold up to which a running subagent holds the handoff back (default 30000);
                             at that size claude-auto hands off anyway and the subagent ends with the old session
  CLAUDE_AUTO_DIR            where notes and auto.log go (default ~/.claude/handoffs/auto)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_CLAUDE         the claude binary (default: claude from PATH)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_COOPERATE=1    opt in to the bundled session-cooperation plugin for interactive work (not bootstrap)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_COOP_DB        absolute registry path (default ~/.claude/cooperation/registry.sqlite3)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_MAKE_CONTEXT   path to make_context.py (default: the newest apana plugin copy)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_GRACE          seconds between the signal and ending claude (default 1.0: the last reply stays on screen)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_KILL_WAIT      seconds claude gets after SIGTERM before SIGKILL (default 5; also when you SIGTERM claude-auto)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_REAP_WAIT      seconds the processes claude left behind get after SIGTERM before SIGKILL (default 1)
  CLAUDE_AUTO_DEBUG=1        log every hook check
Every hook failure is logged to auto.log and the hook exits 0: it never breaks a session.
"""
import fcntl, glob, hashlib, json, os, shlex, shutil, signal, subprocess, sys, tempfile, time, uuid

try:
    import termios
except ImportError:      # not a POSIX terminal; nothing to restore
    termios = None

FIELDS = ("input_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens", "cache_creation_input_tokens")
PASSTHROUGH_FLAGS = {"-p", "--print", "-v", "--version", "-h", "--help", "--bg"}
SUBCOMMANDS = {"agents", "attach", "auth", "auto-mode", "doctor", "gateway", "import", "install", "logs", "mcp",
               "plugin", "plugins", "purge", "respawn", "rm", "setup-token", "stop", "kill", "ultrareview",
               "update", "upgrade"}
STICKY = {"--model": 1, "--permission-mode": 1, "--effort": 1, "--fallback-model": 1, "--agent": 1,
          "--dangerously-skip-permissions": 0, "--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions": 0, "--verbose": 0,
          "--chrome": 0, "--no-chrome": 0, "--ide": 0}
# The rule of the variant-check skill, word for word (a test of that skill pins the two together). Measured once: appended
# to the system prompt it gave 2 of 2 correct runs at effort medium (n = 2), a hook 1 of 3, no rule 1 of 2.
VARIANT_RULE = ("Before writing any matcher or filter over text records, list every distinct variant of the matched token "
                "that actually occurs in the real data and handle each one; after the change, diff your output against "
                "the old output on real data and explain every difference.")
OWN_SYSTEM_PROMPT = ("--append-system-prompt", "--append-system-prompt-file")
# Flags that pick the session a run starts from: 0 = no value, 1 = one value, 2 = a value only when the next argument is not a flag.
PICK_SESSION = {"-c": 0, "--continue": 0, "-r": 2, "--resume": 2, "--from-pr": 2, "--teleport": 2, "--session-id": 1}
# What a terminal UI may leave on after it is killed: cursor, bracketed paste, focus reports, kitty keyboard, mouse.
TERMINAL_RESET = "\x1b[?25h\x1b[?2004l\x1b[?1004l\x1b[<u\x1b[?1000l\x1b[?1002l\x1b[?1003l\x1b[?1006l"
PENDING_CHUNK = 24000    # characters per pending file: one Read in the next session must open it (25000-token cap)
PENDING_LINE = 1800      # the Read tool cuts lines longer than 2000 characters
PENDING_MAX = 30         # pending files per run; more than that is an event storm, not tool results
FAILED_RETRY = 60        # do not retry a failing make_context.py on every tool call


def env_num(name, default, cast=int):
    try:
        return cast(os.environ.get(name, default))
    except ValueError:
        return default


def base_dir():
    return os.environ.get("CLAUDE_AUTO_DIR") or os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/handoffs/auto")


def log(msg):
    line = "%s claude-auto: %s" % (time.strftime("%F %T"), msg)
    try:
        os.makedirs(base_dir(), exist_ok=True)
        with open(os.path.join(base_dir(), "auto.log"), "a") as f:
            f.write(line + "\n")
    except OSError:
        pass
    return line


def say(msg):
    sys.stderr.write("[claude-auto] %s\n" % msg)
    sys.stderr.flush()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hook

def last_usage(lines):
    """Tokens sent with the last main-thread request; records without usage (synthetic) are skipped."""
    for line in reversed(lines):
        if '"usage"' not in line:
            continue
        try:
            r = json.loads(line)
            if r.get("type") != "assistant" or r.get("isSidechain"):
                continue
            u = (r.get("message") or {}).get("usage") or {}
            n = sum(int(u.get(k) or 0) for k in FIELDS)
        except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):
            continue
        if n:
            return n
    return 0


def context_tokens(path, tail=1 << 20):
    """Reads only the end of the transcript (it grows to many MB); the whole file only if the tail has no usage."""
    size = os.path.getsize(path)
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        f.seek(max(0, size - tail))
        data = f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
    lines = data.split("\n")          # not splitlines(): a raw U+2028 inside a JSON string is not a line break
    if size > tail:
        lines = lines[1:]             # the first line is cut at the seek point
    n = last_usage(lines)
    if n or size <= tail:
        return n
    with open(path, errors="replace") as f:
        return last_usage(f.read().split("\n"))


def session_flags(path, tail=1 << 20):
    """Model and effort of the last main-thread request, as the transcript records them (a /model or /effort made
    during the session shows there, a first command line does not know it); absent keys when the tail has neither."""
    def scan(lines):
        for line in reversed(lines):
            if '"usage"' not in line:
                continue
            try:
                r = json.loads(line)
                if r.get("type") != "assistant" or r.get("isSidechain"):
                    continue
                u = (r.get("message") or {}).get("usage") or {}
                if not sum(int(u.get(k) or 0) for k in FIELDS):
                    continue
                found = {"model": r.get("requestedModel"), "effort": r.get("effort")}
            except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):
                continue
            return {k: v for k, v in found.items() if isinstance(v, str) and v and not v.startswith("-")}
        return None

    size = os.path.getsize(path)
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        f.seek(max(0, size - tail))
        lines = f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\n")
    found = scan(lines[1:] if size > tail else lines)      # the first line is cut at the seek point
    if found is None and size > tail:
        with open(path, errors="replace") as f:
            found = scan(f.read().split("\n"))
    return found or {}


def find_make_context():
    p = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_AUTO_MAKE_CONTEXT")
    if p:
        return p
    cache = os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/plugins/cache")
    found = glob.glob(os.path.join(cache, "*/apana/*/skills/compact-handoff/scripts/make_context.py"))
    # the version is the 3rd folder under the cache (<marketplace>/apana/<version>); a split on "/apana/" would also match a home folder named apana
    found.sort(key=lambda f: [int(x) if x.isdigit() else 0 for x in os.path.relpath(f, cache).split("/")[2].split(".")])
    return found[-1] if found else None


def skills_args(script, transcript):
    """The make_context.py options for CLAUDE_AUTO_SKILLS: none (also unset or empty) -> --no-skills; all -> no option;
    NAME,NAME -> --skills with the names that the session loaded. make_context.py stops on a name it did not find, which
    would cost the whole handoff, so the others are left out and logged; with none left, or when --list-skills fails, the
    handoff goes out with --no-skills."""
    want = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_AUTO_SKILLS", "").strip()
    if want.lower() in ("", "none"):
        return ["--no-skills"]
    if want.lower() == "all":
        return []
    names = list(dict.fromkeys(n.strip() for n in want.split(",") if n.strip()))
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, script, transcript, "--list-skills"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=min(30, env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_MAKE_TIMEOUT", 90)))
    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as e:
        log("CLAUDE_AUTO_SKILLS=%s: --list-skills failed (%s); no skills reloaded" % (want, e))
        return ["--no-skills"]
    if r.returncode != 0:
        log("CLAUDE_AUTO_SKILLS=%s: --list-skills exit %s: %s; no skills reloaded" % (want, r.returncode, (r.stderr or r.stdout)[-200:].strip()))
        return ["--no-skills"]
    loaded = [line[len("skill: "):].rsplit(" | ", 1)[0] for line in r.stdout.splitlines()
              if line.startswith("skill: ") and line.endswith(" characters") and " | " in line]
    chosen = [n for n in names if n in loaded]
    if len(chosen) < len(names):
        log("CLAUDE_AUTO_SKILLS: not loaded by this session, left out: %s (loaded: %s)" % (
            ", ".join(n for n in names if n not in loaded), ", ".join(loaded) or "none"))
    return ["--skills", ",".join(chosen)] if chosen else ["--no-skills"]


def safe(s):
    return "".join(c for c in s if c.isalnum() or c in "-_")


def age(path):
    try:
        return time.time() - os.path.getmtime(path)
    except OSError:
        return None


HELD = []        # lock files this hook process holds; the OS drops the flock when the process ends, however it ends


def done_file(run, sid):
    return os.path.join(run, "done-" + safe(sid))


def locked(run, sid):
    """This session was already handed off: the claude behind it has been (or is being) ended."""
    return os.path.exists(done_file(run, sid))


def claim(run, sid):
    """Only one hook process (parallel tool calls) writes the handoff of a session. The claim is an OS lock (flock) held for
    the life of this process: a hook that dies leaves nothing behind to time out, so there is no stale lock to take over."""
    f = open(os.path.join(run, "lock-" + safe(sid)), "a")
    try:
        fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        f.close()
        return False
    if locked(run, sid):             # another hook finished the whole handoff between our check and our lock
        f.close()
        return False
    HELD.append(f)
    return True


def give_up(run, sid):
    """Release the claim so a later trigger may retry, but not within FAILED_RETRY seconds."""
    open(os.path.join(run, "failed-" + safe(sid)), "w").close()
    while HELD:
        HELD.pop().close()


def cooled_down(run):
    a = age(os.path.join(run, "last-handoff"))
    return a is None or a >= env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_COOLDOWN", 60)


def agent_marker(run, agent):
    return os.path.join(run, "agents", safe(agent))


def is_background(path):
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return f.read(2) == "bg"
    except OSError:
        return False


def mark_agent(run, agent, background=False):
    """A subagent is running: its marker is created at SubagentStart and refreshed by each of its tool calls. The marker of a
    background subagent (launch or resume seen in the session's own PostToolUse) also says "bg" in it."""
    path = agent_marker(run, agent)
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    with open(path, "a") as f:
        if background and not is_background(path):
            f.write("bg")
    os.utime(path, None)


def unmark_agent(run, agent, stopped=False):
    """SubagentStop removes the marker. A background one stays as a file, old, so that a SubagentStop that comes late (before
    the next tool call of a resumed subagent) does not make it look like a foreground one; TaskStop (stopped) removes it."""
    path = agent_marker(run, agent)
    try:
        if is_background(path) and not stopped:
            os.utime(path, (0, 0))
        else:
            os.remove(path)
    except OSError:
        pass


def end_foreground_agents(run):
    """At the Stop of the session: a foreground subagent cannot be running, the turn waited for it. One that is still marked
    was interrupted (Esc ends it with no SubagentStop), so it no longer holds the handoff back."""
    folder = os.path.join(run, "agents")
    for name in os.listdir(folder) if os.path.isdir(folder) else []:
        if not is_background(os.path.join(folder, name)):
            unmark_agent(run, name)


def track_subagent_tool(run, d):
    """What a tool call of the main session says about subagents, applied at its PostToolUse so that the order of that event and
    the subagent's own SubagentStart/SubagentStop does not matter. A background launch (isAsync/agentId) and a SendMessage that
    resumes a finished subagent (resumedAgentId; its SubagentStart comes at the same moment) mark it; TaskStop ends one with
    no SubagentStop, so it unmarks it."""
    resp, name = d.get("tool_response"), d.get("tool_name")
    if not isinstance(resp, dict):
        return
    started = resp.get("agentId") if resp.get("isAsync") else resp.get("resumedAgentId") if name == "SendMessage" else None
    if isinstance(started, str) and safe(started):
        mark_agent(run, started, background=True)
    given = d.get("tool_input")
    stopped = (given.get("task_id") if isinstance(given, dict) else None) or resp.get("task_id")
    if name == "TaskStop" and isinstance(stopped, str) and safe(stopped):
        unmark_agent(run, stopped, stopped=True)


def running_agents(run):
    """Markers of subagents that were active within CLAUDE_AUTO_AGENT_IDLE seconds: one whose SubagentStop never came
    (killed, crashed) stops holding the handoff back after that."""
    idle, found = env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_AGENT_IDLE", 900), []
    for name in sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(run, "agents"))) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(run, "agents")) else []:
        a = age(os.path.join(run, "agents", name))
        if a is not None and a < idle:
            found.append(name)
    return found


def deferral_logged(run, agents):
    """True if auto.log already says that this set of subagents holds the handoff back (one line per change, not per event)."""
    path = os.path.join(run, "deferred")
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            if f.read() == ",".join(agents):
                return True
    except OSError:
        pass
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write(",".join(agents))
    return False


def render(v):
    """A tool input or result as text a person can read: strings raw (real newlines), dict keys as [name] headers."""
    if isinstance(v, str):
        return v
    if isinstance(v, dict) and v:
        return "\n".join("[%s]\n%s" % (k, render(x)) for k, x in v.items())
    return json.dumps(v, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)


def pending_text(d):
    """What the transcript does not hold yet for this event, or None."""
    if d.get("hook_event_name") == "PostToolUse" and d.get("tool_response") is not None:
        return "Apel de unealtă: %s (tool_use_id %s), încă nescris în transcript.\n--- input ---\n%s\n--- rezultat ---\n%s\n" % (
            d.get("tool_name"), d.get("tool_use_id"), render(d.get("tool_input")), render(d.get("tool_response")))
    if d.get("hook_event_name") == "Stop" and d.get("last_assistant_message"):
        return "Ultimul răspuns al asistentului, încă nescris în transcript:\n%s\n" % d["last_assistant_message"]
    return None


def split_pending(text):
    """Lines of at most PENDING_LINE characters, grouped into pieces of about PENDING_CHUNK. Nothing is dropped."""
    lines = []
    for line in text.split("\n"):
        while len(line) > PENDING_LINE:
            lines.append(line[:PENDING_LINE])
            line = line[PENDING_LINE:]
        lines.append(line)
    parts, cur, size = [], [], 0
    for line in lines:
        if cur and size + len(line) + 1 > PENDING_CHUNK:
            parts.append("\n".join(cur) + "\n")
            cur, size = [], 0
        cur.append(line)
        size += len(line) + 1
    parts.append("\n".join(cur))
    return parts


def save_pending(run, d):
    """Saves what the transcript does not hold yet for this event into run/pending/, whole, in pieces. Any hook of the
    session calls it: the one that writes the handoff and the ones that lose the claim to it. Returns the files written."""
    text = pending_text(d)
    if text is None:
        return 0
    pdir = os.path.join(run, "pending")
    os.makedirs(pdir, exist_ok=True)
    if len(os.listdir(pdir)) >= PENDING_MAX:
        log("%d pending files already; this event was not saved" % PENDING_MAX)
        return 0
    parts = split_pending(text)
    base = "pending-%s-%019d-%s" % (safe(d.get("session_id") or ""), time.time_ns(),
                                    safe(str(d.get("tool_use_id") or d.get("hook_event_name"))))
    for i, body in enumerate(parts, 1):
        name = base + (".txt" if len(parts) == 1 else "-part%02dof%02d.txt" % (i, len(parts)))
        tmp = os.path.join(pdir, "." + name)
        with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            f.write(body)
        os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(pdir, name))        # atomic: the wrapper never moves half a file
    return len(parts)


def handoff_dir(sid):
    """handoff-<8 hex>-<date>-<random>: unique, and the shape make_context.py looks for when a later handoff keeps this
    one as its parent."""
    h = "".join(c for c in sid[:8].lower() if c in "0123456789abcdef")
    if len(h) < 8:
        h = hashlib.sha1(sid.encode("utf-8", "replace")).hexdigest()[:8]
    os.makedirs(base_dir(), exist_ok=True)
    return tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="handoff-%s-%s-" % (h, time.strftime("%Y%m%d")), dir=base_dir())


def write_signal(run, data):
    tmp = os.path.join(run, "signal.json.tmp")
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(data, f, ensure_ascii=False)
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(run, "signal.json"))      # atomic: the wrapper never reads half a file


def handle(d):
    run = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_AUTO_RUN")
    event, sid, transcript = d.get("hook_event_name"), d.get("session_id") or "", d.get("transcript_path") or ""
    agent = d.get("agent_id")
    if not run or not os.path.isdir(run):
        return None                      # not a claude-auto session
    named = isinstance(agent, str) and bool(safe(agent))
    if event == "SubagentStop":
        if named:
            unmark_agent(run, agent)
        return None
    if event == "SubagentStart" or agent:
        if named:
            mark_agent(run, agent)       # still running
        return None                      # a subagent's event never starts a handoff: continue:false would end that subagent
    if event not in ("PreToolUse", "Stop", "PostToolUse") or not sid or not os.path.isfile(transcript):
        return None
    if os.path.exists(os.path.join(run, "signal.json")):
        save_pending(run, d)             # a handoff is waiting for the wrapper; this event will not reach the transcript either
        return None
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_AUTO_BOOTSTRAP") == "1" and event == "Stop":
        write_signal(run, {"kind": "anchor", "session_id": sid, "cwd": d.get("cwd")})
        return {"systemMessage": "Ancora de cache este pregătită; pornesc sesiunea de lucru."}
    if event == "PostToolUse":
        track_subagent_tool(run, d)
    elif event == "Stop":
        end_foreground_agents(run)
    tokens, threshold = context_tokens(transcript), env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_TOKENS", 150000)
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_AUTO_DEBUG"):
        log("%s %s: %d tokens (threshold %d)" % (event, sid[:8], tokens, threshold))
    margin = max(0, env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_PRETOOL_MARGIN", 30000))
    trigger = max(0, threshold - margin) if event == "PreToolUse" and margin else threshold
    if tokens < trigger:
        return None
    if locked(run, sid):
        return None                      # this session was already handed off
    if not cooled_down(run):
        log("%s: %d tokens but the last handoff is younger than %ds; skipped" % (
            sid[:8], tokens, env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_COOLDOWN", 60)))
        return None
    failed = age(os.path.join(run, "failed-" + safe(sid)))
    if failed is not None and failed < FAILED_RETRY:
        return None
    busy, limit = running_agents(run), threshold + env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_DEFER_EXTRA", 30000)
    if busy and tokens < limit:
        if not deferral_logged(run, busy):
            log("%s: %d tokens >= %d but %d subagent(s) still running (%s); handoff deferred" % (
                sid[:8], tokens, threshold, len(busy), ", ".join(busy)))
        return None
    if busy:
        log("%s: %d tokens >= %d with %d subagent(s) running; handing off anyway, they end with this session" % (
            sid[:8], tokens, limit, len(busy)))
    script = find_make_context()
    if not script or not os.path.isfile(script):
        log("make_context.py not found; skipped")
        return None
    if not claim(run, sid):
        save_pending(run, d)             # another hook is writing the handoff right now; this event is not in its copy
        return None
    out = handoff_dir(sid)
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, script, transcript, out, *skills_args(script, transcript)],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=env_num("CLAUDE_AUTO_MAKE_TIMEOUT", 90))
    except (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as e:
        log("make_context.py failed: %s" % e)
        shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)
        give_up(run, sid)
        return None
    handoff = os.path.join(out, "HANDOFF.md")
    if r.returncode != 0 or not os.path.isfile(handoff):
        log("make_context.py exit %s: %s" % (r.returncode, (r.stderr or r.stdout)[-300:].strip()))
        shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)
        give_up(run, sid)
        return None
    saved = save_pending(run, d)
    if event == "PostToolUse" and not saved:
        log("PostToolUse payload has no tool_response (keys: %s); the last tool result will be missing" % sorted(d))
    write_signal(run, {"event": event, "session_id": sid, "tokens": tokens, "handoff": handoff, "cwd": d.get("cwd"),
                       **session_flags(transcript)})
    open(done_file(run, sid), "w").close()
    open(os.path.join(run, "last-handoff"), "w").close()
    log("%s: %d tokens >= %d; handoff %s" % (sid[:8], tokens, trigger, handoff))
    msg = "Handoff automat la %d tokeni de context: %s. Sesiunea nouă pornește din el." % (tokens, handoff)
    if event == "PreToolUse":
        return {"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PreToolUse", "permissionDecision": "deny",
                                        "permissionDecisionReason": "Handoff automat pregătit; continuă în sesiunea nouă pentru a evita un rezultat de unealtă într-un context aproape plin."}}
    if event == "PostToolUse":
        return {"continue": False, "stopReason": msg, "systemMessage": msg}
    return {"systemMessage": msg}


def hook_main():
    try:
        res = handle(json.load(sys.stdin))
        if res:
            json.dump(res, sys.stdout, ensure_ascii=False)
    except Exception as e:  # a hook must never break the session
        log("unexpected error: %r" % (e,))
    return 0


